WEBVTT

00:31.114 --> 00:33.950
THE TRUNK

00:40.248 --> 00:44.627
5 YEARS AGO

01:14.908 --> 01:17.160
Thanks for letting me say goodbye.

01:18.495 --> 01:20.371
Now what would you like from me,
dear wife?

01:22.082 --> 01:23.750
A wedding and nothing else.

01:32.926 --> 01:34.302
Are you sure you're okay with this?

01:37.055 --> 01:38.181
If it's what you want.

01:40.683 --> 01:41.893
Don't kill my mom, okay?

01:46.397 --> 01:48.024
So I can't put a hit out on her?

01:49.192 --> 01:50.318
Yeah, no hits.

01:53.738 --> 01:54.572
Do you think

01:55.406 --> 01:56.491
she'll come to the ceremony?

01:57.575 --> 01:58.827
No.

01:59.536 --> 02:01.871
Assuming people live to around 80…

02:03.081 --> 02:05.834
Scratch that, we might live even longer.

02:05.917 --> 02:07.961
Assuming we live to around 100,

02:09.879 --> 02:13.591
don't you think you'll get tired
of spending the rest of your life with me?

02:14.300 --> 02:16.302
I'll let you go when you turn 70.

02:19.180 --> 02:20.390
Forty years…

02:22.767 --> 02:24.144
And what should I do after?

02:24.644 --> 02:27.564
You could try spending the next 30 years
with someone else.

02:28.815 --> 02:29.649
A guy.

02:36.156 --> 02:37.615
So do you think

02:39.075 --> 02:40.535
it'll be less lonely by then?

02:42.871 --> 02:43.830
For people, I mean.

02:46.124 --> 02:47.333
Have you been lonely?

02:49.377 --> 02:50.587
A little.

02:52.964 --> 02:54.090
Not right now, though.

02:59.179 --> 03:00.763
The way I see it,

03:02.140 --> 03:03.808
people are either lonely or evil.

03:05.310 --> 03:06.519
If there's one thing

03:07.812 --> 03:08.771
life's taught me,

03:10.273 --> 03:13.026
it's that lonely people
are the ones who get left behind.

03:17.280 --> 03:18.615
In our next lives,

03:19.949 --> 03:21.117
let's not be born.

03:22.952 --> 03:24.078
Let's get left behind.

03:28.666 --> 03:30.335
I'll make sure you're not lonely.

03:31.753 --> 03:35.340
I'll keep you safe,
so you don't have to hide anymore.

03:40.595 --> 03:46.517
THE TRUNK

05:01.092 --> 05:04.387
I watched a documentary
about this ethnic group called the Mosuo.

05:04.470 --> 05:06.764
They live in a matriarchal society
without formal marriage.

05:07.473 --> 05:09.267
Dating's the equivalent of marriage
for them,

05:09.350 --> 05:11.436
and parents don't even know
if their kids are married.

05:11.936 --> 05:16.232
If a child is born, the mother raises it,
and men raise their sisters' children.

05:17.275 --> 05:19.360
Their village looked damn peaceful.

05:20.528 --> 05:21.946
What are you rambling about?

05:23.114 --> 05:25.241
You've never had to check the meter
on a taxi, have you?

05:25.742 --> 05:27.327
I was drinking until 3:00 a.m.,

05:27.410 --> 05:29.954
yet you still called me out here,
so say something.

05:30.455 --> 05:33.166
Or at least catch us some fish
to cook some spicy stew.

05:34.000 --> 05:36.711
Using a living being as bait
to catch another for sport

05:37.712 --> 05:38.546
is cruel.

05:40.214 --> 05:41.507
You're cruel.

05:42.258 --> 05:44.093
I think I want to sleep with that woman.

05:44.177 --> 05:45.094
Which woman?

05:47.472 --> 05:48.681
You mean your wife?

05:57.440 --> 06:00.068
They're not LSD or methamphetamines.

06:00.568 --> 06:03.821
They're zolpidem-type sleeping pills,
doxepin, benzodiazepines,

06:03.905 --> 06:05.740
antidepressants, and anxiolytics.

06:05.823 --> 06:07.658
There was also
some prescription melatonin.

06:08.159 --> 06:12.914
They're all drugs you can have prescribed,
but it's rare to have so many on hand.

06:12.997 --> 06:14.665
Do people ever hide their drugs?

06:15.249 --> 06:17.377
Often, if they're addicted, yes.

06:19.003 --> 06:20.671
Looks like it's going to rain today.

06:21.172 --> 06:23.341
Have a nice day, Ms. Noh.

06:24.634 --> 06:25.468
Thanks.

07:08.052 --> 07:09.554
It's your day off, yet you still work.

07:14.392 --> 07:18.062
I wanted to give this to you that day,
but the timing seemed off.

07:19.272 --> 07:20.857
You always wear the same one, so…

07:28.239 --> 07:29.449
Need help putting it on?

07:32.243 --> 07:34.537
I've gotten used to this one.
I'll put yours on later.

07:41.377 --> 07:43.212
Why'd you act that way at Mr. Han's?

07:45.673 --> 07:46.883
Awkwardly playing house.

07:50.470 --> 07:51.846
I've given it some thought.

07:53.473 --> 07:56.058
I don't think it was because of me
or Han Jeong-won.

07:57.768 --> 07:59.687
Does Ms. Noh In-ji bother you?

08:03.858 --> 08:05.776
I'm used to that house.

08:06.861 --> 08:08.988
I wasn't playing anything.
It was out of habit.

08:09.071 --> 08:11.741
I guess that's one way to explain it.

08:15.912 --> 08:16.746
I'll leave you to it.

09:12.260 --> 09:15.096
YEONHEE UNIVERSITY

09:19.141 --> 09:22.603
HAN JEONG-WON

09:59.098 --> 10:01.475
I feel even more uneasy
now that he's out of sight.

10:01.976 --> 10:04.186
He should have shown up by now.

10:06.814 --> 10:07.940
Eom Tae-seong, I mean.

10:10.026 --> 10:12.945
How are things this time?
Do you like your living arrangement?

10:13.446 --> 10:15.031
This type of marriage is a first for you.

10:15.114 --> 10:17.700
He's not a terminally ill patient
whose days are numbered,

10:18.200 --> 10:21.621
nor a gay guy who needs to get married
because of his parents.

10:22.121 --> 10:24.999
He's also not depressed
and trying to kill himself every day.

10:25.583 --> 10:28.377
He just doesn't need to be
in a contract marriage.

10:29.712 --> 10:33.090
You're damned if they've got issues,
and damned if they don't.

10:34.634 --> 10:35.968
He does have issues.

10:39.597 --> 10:41.182
A drug problem, among other things.

10:44.769 --> 10:46.228
All right, if you say so.

10:47.605 --> 10:49.857
What do you want out of this marriage?

10:52.943 --> 10:55.488
And what can you do for him?

10:57.281 --> 10:58.115
A divorce.

11:02.244 --> 11:03.371
A perfect divorce.

11:07.625 --> 11:09.335
I never thought I'd see the day.

11:09.418 --> 11:12.380
To think you'd find a woman
who's not Lee Seo-yeon.

11:12.922 --> 11:15.508
When you first told me
you were getting married,

11:15.591 --> 11:16.884
I thought you were nuts.

11:17.760 --> 11:20.680
But then, I was lying in bed,
and the notion kind of excited me.

11:20.763 --> 11:23.057
You don't need to waste your energy
looking for a partner,

11:23.557 --> 11:27.061
and you get to enjoy a no-strings marriage
with someone who's a perfect match.

11:27.645 --> 11:30.940
To us married men, that's the dream.
I'm sure even more so for women.

11:31.023 --> 11:34.819
No kids and no in-laws.
Just a safe, casual marriage.

11:34.902 --> 11:36.153
It's too good to be true.

11:37.196 --> 11:39.115
Do you really like that woman?

11:39.198 --> 11:40.366
It's not like that.

11:42.159 --> 11:43.744
- It's just…
- Just?

11:44.745 --> 11:46.622
I've had no trouble sleeping
since she arrived.

11:47.623 --> 11:49.542
I sleep at night
and wake up in the morning.

11:49.625 --> 11:52.294
I'm bothered by the changes she's made,

11:52.378 --> 11:54.463
but more bothered with myself
for being so bothered.

11:56.882 --> 11:58.884
So you want to do it
with a woman who bothers you.

11:58.968 --> 12:00.761
Or maybe I just need a woman
to do it with.

12:00.845 --> 12:04.014
You're not 15. You're over 30.
You should be able to tell the difference.

12:04.098 --> 12:08.310
Why don't you figure out if it's a need
or if you've actually fallen for her?

12:08.394 --> 12:09.729
I haven't fallen for anyone.

12:12.148 --> 12:13.149
I just need a woman.

12:13.232 --> 12:16.277
It's why you don't listen to know-it-alls
who've read just one book

12:16.360 --> 12:17.611
or dated one person.

12:17.695 --> 12:20.906
What would you know?
Lee Seo-yeon's scrambled your brain.

12:39.133 --> 12:39.967
In-ji.

12:46.098 --> 12:46.932
You shop here?

12:48.392 --> 12:49.477
So do I.

12:55.900 --> 12:59.737
Why don't you check if it's just a need
or if you've actually fallen for her?

13:11.999 --> 13:12.958
Where are…

13:27.765 --> 13:29.809
I'm glad I ran into you like this.

13:30.476 --> 13:31.936
Why would you be glad to see me?

13:33.270 --> 13:36.857
I don't have any friends in these parts.
Plus, isn't this fun?

13:37.566 --> 13:39.610
Neither of us has exes,
and we both have partners.

13:40.236 --> 13:43.697
Or maybe you're just glad
to run into a co-worker.

13:45.491 --> 13:46.492
So you knew?

13:47.952 --> 13:50.329
I saw you at the office,
Assistant Manager Yoon.

13:53.290 --> 13:54.583
Here I was thinking only I knew.

13:56.085 --> 13:58.087
Two husbands and two wives.

13:58.671 --> 14:01.632
Like a game of truth
where the real and the fake intertwine.

14:03.342 --> 14:05.553
How about we forge an alliance?

14:07.096 --> 14:09.348
I want to see things through to the end
with Seo-yeon.

14:15.312 --> 14:16.647
Does Ms. Lee Seo-yeon

14:17.940 --> 14:19.316
frequently take medication?

14:20.359 --> 14:21.735
Sleeping pills, for instance.

14:25.030 --> 14:26.323
Are we allies, then?

14:33.747 --> 14:36.625
Would you like to go out for dinner?

14:38.544 --> 14:39.753
You pick the restaurant.

14:42.840 --> 14:43.674
Sure.

14:44.758 --> 14:45.593
Going on a date?

14:47.887 --> 14:49.054
I should get going.

14:50.139 --> 14:51.432
I don't know about you,

14:52.892 --> 14:54.518
but I'm on your side, Ms. Noh.

14:58.814 --> 14:59.773
Best of luck to us.

15:38.646 --> 15:40.439
I didn't expect you'd pick this place.

15:44.109 --> 15:48.030
I figured it would be satisfying
to eat his favorite food in front of him.

15:53.452 --> 15:54.453
Why are you smiling?

15:55.329 --> 15:57.748
I'm wondering if it is just a need.

15:59.375 --> 16:01.794
Do I just need it?
Is there something more to it?

16:02.294 --> 16:03.587
If so, what?

16:07.132 --> 16:08.092
Ignore me.

16:09.385 --> 16:10.219
Dig in.

16:15.057 --> 16:17.059
Isn't seaweed soup mainly for birthdays?

16:17.559 --> 16:19.103
Why does he like it so much?

16:21.814 --> 16:25.526
People who grew up by the seaside
cook this soup with rockfish, not beef.

16:26.026 --> 16:27.444
Once you've had it that way,

16:27.528 --> 16:29.863
its memory follows you
all the way to the city.

16:32.658 --> 16:36.245
You can't replicate that childhood taste,
no matter how hard you try.

16:38.372 --> 16:40.082
But some are beaten
for not getting it right.

16:50.384 --> 16:52.344
We always had seaweed soup at home.

16:53.804 --> 16:56.181
At first, I thought it was
because my father liked it.

16:56.765 --> 16:57.850
I only found out later

16:59.351 --> 17:03.856
that my mom had never even gotten it
after giving birth to me.

17:07.151 --> 17:09.028
My mom never had a mom,

17:10.154 --> 17:12.031
and that haunted her throughout her life.

17:24.918 --> 17:26.503
The day she was beaten by my father

17:26.587 --> 17:28.797
and taken to the hospital
with chipped teeth…

17:31.675 --> 17:34.553
I saw her cook seaweed soup
and eat it in the kitchen in the dark.

17:37.222 --> 17:38.390
All over something like this.

17:40.642 --> 17:43.687
Every time she was hurting,
and every time she was beaten,

17:45.272 --> 17:47.900
maybe she thought it would heal her,

17:49.526 --> 17:52.196
or maybe she believed
her fate was sealed because--

18:04.833 --> 18:06.960
Because no one had ever made her
this soup.

18:11.507 --> 18:14.468
To me, seaweed soup
is a reminder of death.

18:21.809 --> 18:23.435
What does this mean?

18:24.686 --> 18:25.646
It's in the manual.

18:27.898 --> 18:29.650
Something married couples can give.

18:31.693 --> 18:32.528
Moral support.

18:40.911 --> 18:41.912
Think of it as me

18:43.372 --> 18:45.040
holding down a perilla leaf for you.

18:53.966 --> 18:58.720
Back in the day, freedom fighters had
what were called "father-killing pacts."

18:59.221 --> 19:00.264
Have you heard of them?

19:00.973 --> 19:03.767
They would kill each other's
traitorous, pro-Japan fathers

19:04.518 --> 19:07.229
because they couldn't bring themselves
to do it.

19:08.272 --> 19:10.023
A shared division of labor, if you will.

19:10.858 --> 19:12.442
Knowing such a practice existed

19:13.777 --> 19:15.237
is rather comforting to me.

19:21.577 --> 19:22.911
Do you want to do it with me?

19:26.206 --> 19:27.583
I can kill that man…

19:30.210 --> 19:31.670
and you can kill my mom.

19:56.945 --> 19:58.280
Is my father fuming?

19:59.489 --> 20:01.033
No, I'm almost there.

20:01.116 --> 20:02.201
I'm going in now.

20:02.284 --> 20:03.118
Okay, see you.

20:04.077 --> 20:05.037
Mr. Oh Hyeon-cheol?

20:05.787 --> 20:06.663
Yes, and you are?

20:07.998 --> 20:09.708
Your wife ordered
your father's rice cakes.

20:10.209 --> 20:12.878
- We met at a Heritage Lounge gathering.
- I see, thanks.

20:12.961 --> 20:13.921
I'm a fan of yours.

20:15.964 --> 20:18.842
I listen to every release
from your record label.

20:18.926 --> 20:21.094
Thank you, but I really must run.

20:22.471 --> 20:23.972
Producer Han Jeong-won.

20:27.643 --> 20:30.604
I've loved his work in particular.

20:32.064 --> 20:32.898
Right.

20:36.360 --> 20:38.445
- I'm with the Oh Hyeon-cheol party.
- This way.

20:42.074 --> 20:43.033
How was your day?

20:46.954 --> 20:50.082
Spouses often ask things like,
"What did you get up to today?"

20:53.293 --> 20:54.169
I went fishing.

20:55.462 --> 20:57.297
Do you like fishing?

20:58.215 --> 20:59.049
No.

21:00.133 --> 21:00.968
Why not?

21:01.051 --> 21:03.512
I have pet goldfish.
Fishing reminds me of them.

21:08.058 --> 21:09.309
Why the look?

21:13.438 --> 21:16.483
Don't you feel bad for your goldfish
when you grill fish?

21:17.901 --> 21:19.528
I can stop making fish if you like.

21:20.320 --> 21:21.863
You even know how to make threats.

21:25.367 --> 21:26.618
What did you do today?

21:29.621 --> 21:31.999
You're the one who said
spouses ask such things.

21:33.709 --> 21:34.710
I did this and that.

21:35.585 --> 21:39.589
Small but important things
that aren't apparent but need to be done.

21:42.968 --> 21:44.886
I had to run the dryer because it rained.

21:45.387 --> 21:47.389
I'd wanted to dry our sheets in the sun.

21:52.352 --> 21:53.312
It's comforting.

21:58.817 --> 22:01.153
I don't know why,
but when you say things like that…

22:01.862 --> 22:04.656
I like the things you say sometimes.

22:05.574 --> 22:08.243
It's not even any words in particular.
It just feels like…

22:10.245 --> 22:12.205
you're undoing the buttons
that were fastened wrong

22:13.165 --> 22:15.667
and re-buttoning them correctly,
one by one.

22:17.627 --> 22:19.212
Do you struggle with buttons?

22:20.505 --> 22:22.132
I used to when I was younger.

22:23.675 --> 22:25.385
Sometimes I screwed up on purpose

22:26.595 --> 22:28.638
just to see the spark come back
to my mother's eyes.

22:30.223 --> 22:31.850
"Look at your shirt," she'd say.

22:35.395 --> 22:38.690
She'd sit down, back to her old self,
and redo my buttons one by one.

22:44.905 --> 22:47.157
You have a way of disarming people.

22:47.657 --> 22:49.493
I keep sharing these silly stories.

22:49.576 --> 22:50.994
I'm not saying that's why I…

22:52.245 --> 22:54.456
kissed you or anything.

23:16.895 --> 23:18.271
So you do know how to do housework.

23:19.815 --> 23:22.067
My father didn't like
having people in the house.

23:22.150 --> 23:24.444
I don't want to take after him,
but I'm the same.

23:25.445 --> 23:27.614
I pretty much lived alone
for about ten years.

23:28.532 --> 23:32.077
I didn't replace any furniture.
I just cleaned and organized.

23:37.457 --> 23:39.376
Whenever a new piece of furniture arrives,

23:39.876 --> 23:43.380
it's like a battle,
so it takes time for me to get used to it.

23:46.633 --> 23:47.926
You must feel the same about me.

23:51.513 --> 23:53.098
You have a knack for housework.

23:57.561 --> 24:00.147
Why does your mom have to die?

24:02.441 --> 24:05.485
It may be useful to know
if we ever decide on that labor exchange.

24:07.279 --> 24:09.030
You don't have to say
if you don't want to.

24:10.866 --> 24:11.700
My mom…

24:13.827 --> 24:14.828
ruined my marriage

24:16.746 --> 24:18.540
and killed him.

25:03.210 --> 25:04.044
You killed them?

25:06.254 --> 25:07.797
Holy crap!

25:08.298 --> 25:09.966
What are you doing here so early?

25:10.467 --> 25:11.343
Why are you here?

25:11.885 --> 25:14.638
It's much stranger
you're here at this hour, Ms. Do-dam.

25:14.721 --> 25:16.097
For fuck's sake.

25:16.723 --> 25:20.727
You try raising them, then!
Let's see how long they last.

25:21.728 --> 25:23.605
Try keeping them alive in this house.

25:23.688 --> 25:27.651
With the right kind of care,
these guys can outlive dogs.

25:28.360 --> 25:29.569
Don't say anything, okay?

25:31.363 --> 25:33.114
They keep her attached to this place.

25:33.198 --> 25:34.449
If she finds out they died,

25:35.575 --> 25:36.826
imagine how devastated she'd be.

25:36.910 --> 25:39.037
It's almost like
you actually care about her.

25:39.120 --> 25:40.622
Snitch, and you'll pay for it.

25:41.206 --> 25:42.040
Okay, fine.

25:46.753 --> 25:49.589
The punk who owns this place
is still alive, isn't he?

25:52.008 --> 25:53.218
He'll be back, won't he?

25:55.262 --> 25:56.096
Yes.

25:57.055 --> 25:58.223
He's alive, apparently.

25:59.140 --> 26:02.185
We thought he was dead,
but apparently, he's still alive.

26:24.583 --> 26:25.542
How have you been?

26:27.335 --> 26:29.254
So you'd rather not be
a rude-ass southerner.

26:32.340 --> 26:33.341
I've been all right.

26:35.427 --> 26:36.344
Have you eaten?

26:52.485 --> 26:54.654
Is your husband still against it?

26:57.741 --> 26:59.534
What about keeping the next one?

27:03.288 --> 27:05.665
The gynecologist told me
that I can't have kids.

27:06.666 --> 27:08.460
They say I was born with a weak uterus.

27:10.629 --> 27:14.758
I've lost contact with my younger sibling.
No wonder I didn't dream of their corpse.

27:15.800 --> 27:16.801
They're probably dead.

27:18.261 --> 27:19.846
Now it's just me and this baby,

27:20.972 --> 27:22.349
truly alone in the world.

27:26.394 --> 27:27.646
I want this baby.

27:31.274 --> 27:33.068
NM won't sit idly by.

27:35.487 --> 27:39.366
If the client doesn't want the baby,
the company has to pay an exorbitant fee.

27:41.242 --> 27:42.410
So before that happens…

27:50.168 --> 27:53.421
These are the brokers who kept me updated.
He's still over there.

27:53.505 --> 27:57.133
He worked for a small trading company
that imported and exported goods to Korea.

27:57.634 --> 27:59.928
Now he works as a tour guide.

28:00.887 --> 28:02.097
He sells fish tanks too.

28:03.932 --> 28:04.849
Ridiculous, isn't it?

28:05.475 --> 28:06.309
Fish tanks.

28:07.435 --> 28:10.980
I get the feeling
that he's going to come back someday.

28:12.649 --> 28:14.567
Whether he'll come back to you
is another story.

28:22.826 --> 28:23.910
Where are you headed?

28:28.206 --> 28:29.040
Home.

28:48.893 --> 28:50.311
Want to watch a movie together?

29:00.947 --> 29:01.781
Isn't this nice?

29:02.949 --> 29:04.659
Lee Seo-yeon worked on this place.

29:05.410 --> 29:07.495
How did your father's birthday go?

29:07.579 --> 29:09.080
The rice cakes saved it.

29:09.831 --> 29:12.459
The guy who made them seemed to know you.

29:12.542 --> 29:13.376
Who?

29:13.460 --> 29:15.587
I heard he went
to a Heritage Lounge gathering

29:15.670 --> 29:16.713
and is a fan of yours.

29:17.213 --> 29:18.840
Who knew you had fans?

29:22.844 --> 29:23.845
Sure.

29:28.183 --> 29:29.184
Hello, Seo-yeon.

29:29.893 --> 29:30.894
I'll be going now.

29:31.478 --> 29:34.063
Are you here because of the remodeling?

29:35.523 --> 29:37.150
You seem happy about something.

29:45.867 --> 29:46.701
Thanks.

29:47.285 --> 29:49.662
Want to grab something to eat?
I happen to be free.

29:52.415 --> 29:54.125
It's okay if you have an appointment.

29:54.209 --> 29:56.169
Sorry, but I have somewhere to be.

29:57.754 --> 29:59.923
How about tomorrow
at a time that works for you?

30:00.799 --> 30:01.800
Sure, let's do that.

30:02.717 --> 30:03.802
All right, then.

30:12.769 --> 30:16.105
I had to get the tickets last minute,
and this was our only option.

30:17.190 --> 30:18.650
I like these kinds of movies.

30:51.933 --> 30:53.142
Why aren't you watching?

30:56.980 --> 30:57.939
Because I'm scared.

30:59.941 --> 31:01.484
I can't stomach movies like these.

31:33.892 --> 31:34.809
Is it very scary?

31:48.323 --> 31:51.159
The person you have called
is currently unavailable…

31:51.242 --> 31:53.953
HAN JEONG-WON

31:57.248 --> 31:59.834
The person you have called
is currently unavailable…

32:21.397 --> 32:22.899
Don't horror movies scare you?

32:24.567 --> 32:25.401
They do.

32:27.946 --> 32:29.364
You sure didn't look scared.

32:31.491 --> 32:33.910
In a way, horror movies can be comforting.

32:34.869 --> 32:36.329
It's a relief knowing

32:37.413 --> 32:40.416
that my life is safer
than what happens in those movies.

32:42.460 --> 32:44.545
I hear that's why
people watch horror movies.

32:47.256 --> 32:49.300
Is there a reason
you need to feel that way?

32:51.678 --> 32:52.512
At times, yes.

32:55.139 --> 32:56.432
We have that in common.

33:01.312 --> 33:03.064
I'm glad you asked me to a movie.

33:03.773 --> 33:05.400
I liked the choice of movie too.

33:12.198 --> 33:14.242
I guess today was one of those days
you needed relief.

33:17.245 --> 33:18.079
A little.

33:20.164 --> 33:20.999
Why?

33:23.459 --> 33:25.670
You know that man
my mom supposedly killed?

33:27.213 --> 33:28.214
There's a chance

33:29.841 --> 33:32.051
I'll be meeting him soon.

33:41.477 --> 33:42.645
I'm not sure

33:44.230 --> 33:45.857
if this is the right time to say this…

33:52.363 --> 33:54.323
but I think I want to sleep with you.

33:59.037 --> 34:00.913
I wish I could sugarcoat it,

34:01.748 --> 34:03.499
but that would sound too contrived.

34:06.544 --> 34:08.713
I'm telling you this
instead of holding it in…

34:11.174 --> 34:13.968
because I'm worried nothing will happen
if I don't tell you now.

34:15.678 --> 34:18.681
I'm always subtracting things in life.

34:19.182 --> 34:20.767
I've subtracted and subtracted,

34:21.726 --> 34:23.978
and finally ended up
with a rather simple equation…

34:25.897 --> 34:27.523
but I can't figure out where you fit in.

34:31.235 --> 34:33.154
I can't tell if I want to sleep with you…

34:36.032 --> 34:38.409
simply because you're a woman,
or because I like you.

34:40.870 --> 34:41.704
I hope…

34:44.540 --> 34:46.751
it's simply because you're a woman.

34:55.885 --> 34:57.053
I'll keep that in mind.

35:24.747 --> 35:27.708
WIFE

35:50.231 --> 35:51.357
Where's the whiskey?

36:10.042 --> 36:11.127
Drink it slowly.

36:15.173 --> 36:16.048
Pour me another.

36:16.883 --> 36:18.759
I found it for you. Pour it yourself!

36:18.843 --> 36:20.094
You do it!

36:25.933 --> 36:29.145
I should have at least one person
I can control however I'd like.

36:30.396 --> 36:31.480
That person's you.

36:36.402 --> 36:38.362
Don't you care who I am,

36:39.405 --> 36:41.199
or what I used to do before this?

36:41.782 --> 36:43.534
None of that matters to me.

36:44.160 --> 36:46.370
Just because I like you
doesn't mean I'm yours.

36:48.581 --> 36:49.415
On the contrary,

36:50.499 --> 36:51.709
you are mine.

36:53.252 --> 36:54.128
At least for a year.

37:04.764 --> 37:06.891
Stop drinking.
You look pathetic enough already.

37:23.366 --> 37:24.200
Sir.

37:25.451 --> 37:26.786
They've identified the body.

37:27.828 --> 37:28.663
Eom Tae-seong?

37:28.746 --> 37:31.499
Eom Tae-seong, 36-year-old male.

37:31.582 --> 37:34.168
History of mental illness
and past hospitalizations.

37:35.461 --> 37:38.214
The fatal wound was to his chest,
and he also has a leg wound.

37:45.304 --> 37:46.138
Oh dear.

37:47.598 --> 37:49.892
Am I going to have to buy a new batch?

37:51.519 --> 37:52.728
They don't look so good.

39:13.851 --> 39:16.020
How's he connected to the trunk's owner?

39:17.063 --> 39:19.148
He isn't.
They didn't live anywhere near each other.

39:20.691 --> 39:22.068
So it was a simple robbery?

39:22.735 --> 39:24.236
That's what it looks like.

39:24.987 --> 39:26.447
Why would a thief steal a trunk,

39:26.530 --> 39:28.991
then get on a boat
in the middle of the night?

39:29.075 --> 39:30.659
Taxis and buses are everywhere.

39:31.160 --> 39:32.703
Maybe it was to avoid cameras.

39:32.787 --> 39:35.331
The CCTV wires were cut, remember?

39:35.414 --> 39:37.375
The dead guy might not have known that.

39:39.001 --> 39:41.462
Did you find any signs
boats were used there?

39:41.545 --> 39:43.339
Did anyone hear any engine sounds?

39:43.422 --> 39:45.591
We're still questioning people, but no.

39:47.343 --> 39:50.221
Our victim had
an impressive criminal record.

39:51.389 --> 39:53.349
Like what? What's the most recent offense?

39:54.141 --> 39:54.975
Stalking.

39:55.518 --> 39:59.313
He was arrested for repeated stalking,
but his sentence was reduced.

39:59.397 --> 40:03.359
Before that, he was fined and served time
for stalking. He's a seven-time offender.

40:03.442 --> 40:04.527
Who was he stalking?

40:10.741 --> 40:13.077
What is it? Just tell me.

40:13.869 --> 40:17.289
It's Mr. Han Jeong-won's wife.
Why's her name here?

40:18.040 --> 40:18.916
Ms. Lee Seo-yeon?

40:19.417 --> 40:22.795
No, not the ex-wife. The other one.

40:22.878 --> 40:24.755
His common-law wife, Ms. Noh In-ji.

40:25.464 --> 40:28.050
Contact Ms. Noh In-ji,
and get me Mr. Han's address.

41:18.309 --> 41:20.811
- Do you have a Heritage Lounge gathering?
- Yes.

41:23.022 --> 41:23.856
See you, then.

41:32.364 --> 41:33.908
I only make mistakes when you're around.

41:34.783 --> 41:37.828
I don't let my guard down
around anyone else.

41:46.629 --> 41:47.546
Have a good time.

41:50.925 --> 41:51.842
Try to behave.

41:53.886 --> 41:55.095
Watch out for cars.

41:58.098 --> 41:59.099
And hurry back.

42:19.912 --> 42:23.082
I just got this mugwort tea,
and I wanted to show it off.

42:28.754 --> 42:30.631
It's so good. Don't you agree?

42:31.340 --> 42:32.174
It sure is.

42:33.342 --> 42:35.594
I heard you had a gathering
at Jeong-won's house.

42:36.845 --> 42:38.013
That's right.

42:38.097 --> 42:41.141
The ex-husband, current husband,
ex-wife, and current wife were all there?

42:42.059 --> 42:45.312
Why didn't you invite us
to such a special occasion?

42:49.233 --> 42:51.360
We had a light meal, then called it a day.

42:51.443 --> 42:53.195
It's nice you're all getting along.

42:55.614 --> 42:57.575
Ma'am, will someone else be joining us?

42:58.534 --> 42:59.743
I asked Ms. In-ji to join us.

43:01.203 --> 43:04.665
I was supposed to meet her this afternoon,
but I had to reschedule.

43:05.374 --> 43:07.585
You're all acquainted,
so I thought it'd be fine.

43:08.460 --> 43:11.130
If it makes you uncomfortable,
I can set up a separate meeting.

43:11.630 --> 43:13.257
I'm okay with it.

43:13.966 --> 43:15.301
You don't mind, do you?

43:15.801 --> 43:17.928
I mean,
you've already had dinner together.

43:39.366 --> 43:42.119
Ma'am, your guest is here.

43:48.167 --> 43:49.293
You're here.

43:52.796 --> 43:53.714
Hello.

43:53.797 --> 43:56.258
Apologies.
I already had an appointment with them.

43:56.925 --> 43:59.428
And I thought it might be nice
to meet everyone all at once.

44:00.304 --> 44:01.597
Would you be okay with that?

44:04.558 --> 44:05.392
Of course.

44:20.199 --> 44:22.951
I thought we might enjoy some tea.

44:23.702 --> 44:25.829
It's been a while, Ms. In-ji.
I'm Kang Yoon-a.

44:26.872 --> 44:28.290
Of course, I remember you.

44:33.337 --> 44:34.421
How have you been?

44:35.964 --> 44:39.009
Sorry for not being in touch
since you had us over. Is Jeong-won…

44:43.472 --> 44:45.099
Is Mr. Han also doing well?

44:46.642 --> 44:47.476
He is.

44:47.559 --> 44:49.770
And is your husband doing well?

44:56.402 --> 44:58.696
Were you with him yesterday by any chance?

44:59.738 --> 45:03.534
I needed to discuss soundproofing material
for his studio, but I couldn't reach him.

45:04.618 --> 45:08.831
He asked for a specific one,
but there are many with the same name.

45:09.456 --> 45:11.750
It's probably because
we were at the movies yesterday.

45:12.876 --> 45:14.628
His phone must have been on silent.

45:16.046 --> 45:16.880
I see.

45:25.639 --> 45:27.433
What kind of tea do you like?

45:27.516 --> 45:31.311
We were having some mugwort tea
that I just got, but there are others too.

45:32.604 --> 45:33.939
How about raspberry tea?

45:34.940 --> 45:37.192
I tried it on my last visit,
and it was great.

45:38.736 --> 45:40.362
I think it would suit Ms. In-ji.

45:44.324 --> 45:45.200
Would that be okay?

45:47.745 --> 45:48.787
Yes.

46:07.097 --> 46:08.182
How is it?

46:10.893 --> 46:13.061
I hope you like it,
even though I recommended it.

46:14.980 --> 46:15.814
I like it.

46:17.858 --> 46:18.942
I like berries.

46:25.908 --> 46:27.743
By the way, what are beets good for?

46:29.495 --> 46:32.372
Right, I heard that beets
are so good for you.

46:33.791 --> 46:35.959
They're great to drink in the morning.

46:36.585 --> 46:37.544
I see.

46:39.379 --> 46:40.881
I've always wondered…

46:44.301 --> 46:45.844
why people drink that stuff.

46:58.774 --> 47:02.277
Why doesn't Ms. In-ji join us
at the Heritage Lounge gatherings?

47:03.195 --> 47:06.323
I would love that.
She's Jeong-won's wife, after all.

47:09.993 --> 47:10.828
Of course.

47:14.540 --> 47:15.624
I'm all for it,

47:16.625 --> 47:18.085
if you're worried what I might think.

47:22.172 --> 47:23.006
I see.

47:24.508 --> 47:25.759
I won't worry, then.

47:38.063 --> 47:39.231
Where did you park?

47:39.898 --> 47:41.650
A public parking lot over there.

47:42.526 --> 47:44.820
Park on the other side next time.
It's easier.

47:46.071 --> 47:46.905
How about you?

47:47.865 --> 47:50.951
I have another class this afternoon
since the kids will be home late.

47:51.910 --> 47:52.744
In that case,

47:53.620 --> 47:54.872
it was nice seeing you.

47:56.081 --> 47:57.165
Likewise.

48:12.598 --> 48:14.308
Jesus Christ, that was exhausting.

48:15.559 --> 48:16.768
Holy hell.

48:58.936 --> 49:02.105
Are you all right?
A cat came out of nowhere.

49:09.071 --> 49:10.572
We'll need to tow your car.

49:18.622 --> 49:21.416
I've never caused an accident like this,
even when I was a new driver.

49:21.917 --> 49:23.669
I'll make sure the car is repaired.

49:25.796 --> 49:27.631
I'll ask Mr. Han to handle it.

49:27.714 --> 49:31.259
I know, but I'll do it myself.
It was my fault.

49:31.843 --> 49:33.637
Let's keep this a secret.

49:34.721 --> 49:35.555
A secret?

49:40.394 --> 49:41.436
You don't like secrets?

49:43.230 --> 49:45.315
I just don't see
why it should be a secret.

49:48.402 --> 49:49.861
So you're not a fan of secrets.

49:50.612 --> 49:53.198
Fine, then. Why hide something like this?

49:55.075 --> 49:58.370
But aren't some things better kept hidden?

50:00.664 --> 50:03.917
For instance,
the fact that you and Jeong-won

50:05.252 --> 50:06.878
are in a temporary marriage.

50:12.884 --> 50:14.136
You don't seem surprised.

50:15.679 --> 50:18.140
I was told the ex-wife
was the one who requested it from NM.

50:19.016 --> 50:20.267
You're missing the point.

50:20.809 --> 50:24.438
The point is,
I'm the one who chose you, Ms. Noh In-ji.

50:28.608 --> 50:31.778
I was told there was no chance
you two would ever match,

50:31.862 --> 50:33.155
so I figured it'd never happen.

50:34.406 --> 50:37.075
But your decision to take the job
has made things fun for me.

50:47.085 --> 50:49.337
You're the one who picked me?

50:51.131 --> 50:52.132
That's right.

50:53.383 --> 50:55.969
Why go to such lengths
to torment Mr. Han Jeong-won?

51:08.523 --> 51:11.109
Why go to such lengths
to torment Mr. Han Jeong-won?

51:12.486 --> 51:14.821
Do you know the fable
of the scorpion and the frog?

51:14.905 --> 51:17.365
After stinging the frog
that saves its life,

51:17.949 --> 51:19.701
the scorpion explains
it couldn't help itself.

51:19.785 --> 51:20.869
It's just in its nature.

51:21.995 --> 51:24.623
Everyone's got their own point of view.

51:27.876 --> 51:30.921
You seem to be
a very diligent person, Ms. In-ji.

51:31.004 --> 51:34.049
You prepare his breakfast
and even debone his fish.

51:34.549 --> 51:38.470
Thank you for taking care of Jeong-won
in ways I never could have imagined.

51:39.471 --> 51:41.890
Please be happy for this one year.

51:42.474 --> 51:45.977
I may be punishing Jeong-won,
but I'm also giving him some time off.

51:49.356 --> 51:51.191
By the way, what are beets good for?

51:55.612 --> 51:58.865
The point is,
I'm the one who chose you, Ms. Noh In-ji.

53:24.618 --> 53:25.452
Are you awake?

53:27.746 --> 53:29.956
I moved you
because you seemed uncomfortable.

53:34.127 --> 53:35.629
Are you done subtracting?

53:37.547 --> 53:38.673
I still don't have an answer.

53:40.967 --> 53:43.470
Never mind. I was talking nonsense.

53:51.895 --> 53:53.063
I'll keep that in mind.

57:33.408 --> 57:36.619
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
